# Deep-Sight  frontend build configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` (or set these in your host's environment settings) BEFORE `npm run build`.
# Vite inlines VITE_* variables at build time, so changing this needs a rebuild  it is not
# read at runtime.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_BASE  where the backend lives.
#
# Leave BLANK when the backend is reachable on the same origin as the page, i.e. your
# host rewrites /api and /ws to it (nginx proxy_pass, Vercel/Netlify rewrites, Caddy,
# or the FastAPI app serving dist/ itself). This is the simplest deployment.
#
#   VITE_API_BASE=
#
# Set an ABSOLUTE URL, no trailing slash, when the backend is on a different host.
# The WebSocket URL is derived from it automatically (https -> wss), so serve the API
# over HTTPS if the frontend is on HTTPS, or the browser will block the socket.
#
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://deep-sight-api.example.com
#
# The backend must also allow the frontend's origin via CORS. backend/main.py currently
# sets allow_origins=["*"], which is fine for a demo and should be tightened for anything
# longer-lived.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_API_BASE=
